  "id": "hip-abduction",
  "name": "Hip Abduction",
  "definition": "A strict open-chain hip-abduction isolation. The roster owns the original pressure-biofeedback side-lying cuff-weight fixture and one exact bilateral Technogym seated isotonic-machine fixture at eighty degrees of hip flexion. Their support, endpoint, knee posture, load interface, path constraint, and cadence remain branch-specific. Gluteus medius is primary and tensor fasciae latae is secondary. Other machines, standing, band, cable, bodyweight-only, rotated, clamshell, lateral-walk, closed-chain, and multi-joint variants remain outside this contract.",
  "evidenceRefs": [
    "arnold-2010-lower-limb",
    "mcbeth-2012-side-lying-hip-abduction",
    "brandt-2013-machine-hip-abduction-adduction"
  ],
